Unpatched SLASH'EM

Submachine gun, a few bullets:  Less then 40 weight, one handed.
Rocket launcher + rocket:	950 weight, two handed.

Damage:  Roughly the same (add either a 25 weight frag grenade or a 
	a 7 weight /oFireball if you want to mimic the fire damage).

------------------------------------------------------------------------

I was taking a break from nethack recently and am trying to ascend my
first slash'em character (an undead slayer).  Its been rather fun, but
I've found that certain firearms are basically worthless due to their
weight.

Wrote up a quick patch to change certain weights around.  The heavy
machine gun was adjusted from 500 wgt to 65 weight, the sniper rifle was
adjusted from 50 to 35, auto shotgun from 60 to 40, and the rocket
launcher was adjusted from an astonishing 750 weight to 80 weight.
( All of these weapons are still 2-handed weapons, the ROF, +Hit, and
range are still the same. )

In addition, rockets are now 30 weight, while grenades and sticks of
dynamite are 15.  [ I'm debating if grenades and dynamite is too low --
should they be 25 instead? ]

Hopefully, this will turn a few rather useless weapons into a valid
option for some players, assuming they want to forgo a shield or
two-weaponing.

Have fun, and report any problems.  I'll be playing without the patch
for a bit, as I attempt a "vanilla" slash'em ascension.


